Remove the duplicate doca_mmap_set_memrange() call in create_mmap()

create_mmap() sets the memory range in one of two branches:
doca_mmap_set_dmabuf_memrange() when doca_gpu_dmabuf_fd() succeeds, or
doca_mmap_set_memrange() (nvidia-peermem) when it fails. It then calls
doca_mmap_set_memrange() again outside the branches. doca_mmap.h documents
both setters as "can be done only once", and the second call fails with
"Mmap memory range address can only be set once" (DOCA_ERROR_NOT_PERMITTED),
so create_mmap() returns an error without logging it.

Reported upstream: https://github.com/NVIDIA-DOCA/doca-samples/issues/7
Unchanged in DOCA 3.0.0 to 3.5.0.

Apply in samples/doca_gpunetio/ with: patch -p1

--- a/rdma_common.c
+++ b/rdma_common.c
@@ -603,10 +603,6 @@
 		}
 	}

-	result = doca_mmap_set_memrange(mmap_obj->mmap, mmap_obj->memrange_addr, mmap_obj->memrange_len);
-	if (result != DOCA_SUCCESS)
-		goto error;
-
 	result = doca_mmap_add_dev(mmap_obj->mmap, mmap_obj->doca_device);
 	if (result != DOCA_SUCCESS)
 		goto error;
